│  import sys                                                        │
│  [/original]                                                       │
│  [patched]                                                         │
│  import sys                                                        │
│  [/patched]                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This patch adds a check within the process_input method to see if  │
│ the user entered anything. If the input string is empty (meaning   │
│ the user just pressed Enter), the sys.exit() function is called to │
│ terminate the program. I have also added the import statement for  │
│ sys to ensure it is available. This addresses the core issue of    │
│ the program failing to exit when the user presses Enter.           │
